  "description": "The s.16(4) expiry at every boundary that moves it: 31-March against 01-April (one day apart, one year apart in expiry), a claim ON 30-November against one on 01-December (the date itself is INCLUSIVE), a DEBIT NOTE whose own date fixes its financial year rather than the underlying invoice's (de-linked w.e.f. 01-01-2021), and an annual return filed early, which pulls the expiry forward. Without it, ITC is either claimed after it has died or thrown away while it is still alive — and neither is recoverable once the return is filed.",
